config.prompt:
Do the next meaningful step on this task, then stop and report.

Task:
{{inputs.task}}

Done when:
{{inputs.exit_condition}}

Previous step:
{{last.output.summary}}

Cite evidence a verifier can check without asking you: paths, commands, their actual output. An independent judge closes every step — it never sees this instruction or anything you say about your own work, only the task and the tool output.

Set meaningful_progress to false when there is genuinely nothing left worth doing. That is how the loop ends, and claiming progress to look busy keeps it running on the user's money.

Return JSON: {"summary": string, "meaningful_progress": boolean, "evidence": string}
